  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of essential and lifesaving WASH and Education services to flood affected population across nine states</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $1.7 million UNICEF project is to provide flood-affected people with life-saving support in the water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) and education clusters. In terms of WASH support, UNICEF will conduct critical repairs to improve the water supply infrastructure, construct emergency latrines, provide hygiene items and implement hygiene promotion campaigns, among other activities, reaching a total of 50,000 people, including 14,330 women, 11,218 girls, and 5,000 people with disabilities. In terms of education support, UNICEF will repair education facilities and damaged equipment, set up temporary learning spaces, and distribute essential education and recreational materials, among other activities, to support 12,365 people, including 12,000 school-aged children (4,000 boys and 8,000 girls) of which 1,200 are living with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
